My glass of water is empty.
I stay comfortably seated at my table.
But it is time.
I want to leave now.
I look for the waiter.
He is working at the counter.
He looks in my direction.
I raise my hand slightly.
He sees me and immediately comes to my table.
"Excuse me," I say.
"Could I pay, please?"
"Yes, of course," the waiter answers politely.
He is now standing right in front of me.
He has a small leather wallet in his hand.
I open my backpack.
I look for my money.
I am ready for the bill.
